1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
An integral counts area below the axis as negative.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
x squared minus 2x is below the axis between 0 and 2, above it after 2.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,500
The two pieces cancel: minus 4/3 plus 4/3 is 0.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,000
The geometric area of the same region is 8/3, about 2.666667.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Between two curves, integrate the upper one minus the lower one.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:45,000
On 0 to 1, y equals x sits above y equals x squared.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,500
Find the crossings first: they are the limits.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:00,000
The area is 32/3, about 10.666667.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
The same region can be sliced two ways.

10
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,000
A horizontal slice needs a curve read backwards, as x of y.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,500
Vertical slicing gives 1/3.

12
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:30,000
Horizontal slicing gives 1/3 as well.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,500
With a moving upper limit the integral becomes a function.

14
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:45,000
Its difference quotient falls onto the integrand.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,500
The derivative of the accumulated area is the current height.

16
00:01:52,500 --> 00:02:00,000
Adding a constant changes the level, never the rate.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,500
Integrating a rate gives the net change, not the total activity.

18
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:15,000
This velocity is negative in the middle of the interval.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,500
The three pieces are 4/3, minus 4/3 and 4/3, so the displacement is 4/3.

20
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:30,000
Distance travelled takes absolute values, and comes to 4.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,500
The average value of a function is its integral over the width.

22
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:45,000
It is the height of the rectangle with the same area.

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,500
For sine over 0 to pi the average is 2 over pi, about 0.636620.

24
00:02:52,500 --> 00:03:00,000
Two points attain it: 0.690107 and 2.451486.

25
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,500
A probability is an area under a density.

26
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:15,000
That area is a difference of two values of the distribution function.

27
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:22,500
Exponential with rate 0.5: the probability between 1 and 3 is 0.383400.

28
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:30,000
Normal between minus 1 and 1 is 0.682689; uniform between 1 and 3 is 0.5.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:37,500
The same three readings work on any rate graph.

30
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:45,000
Over 0 to 2 pi the total is 4 pi, about 12.566371.

31
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:52,500
The average rate is exactly 2.

32
00:03:52,500 --> 00:04:00,000
An average of ones and zeros is a fraction of time.

33
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,500
Trap one: the signed integral offered where the area was asked for.

34
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:15,000
Trap two: a crossing that was not used to split the integral.

35
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,500
Trap three: the width divisor left out of an average value.

36
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:30,000
Trap four: the wrong variable, or limits left in the old one.

37
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:37,500
First name the type: one of five.

38
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:45,000
For an area, find the crossings before the antiderivative.

39
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:52,500
For a rate, ask net change or total before integrating.

40
00:04:52,500 --> 00:05:00,000
Bound the answer before you look at the options.

